        "q_how_do_i_know_which_skin_type_i_am": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know which skin type I am?",
            "answer": "<p>The <a href=\"/pages/find-your-skin-type\">skin type finder</a> asks two questions about how your skin behaves and points you at one of five types. It takes a couple of minutes.</p> <p>If you would rather work it out yourself, the short version is this. Skin that feels tight and flakes is dry. Skin that shines by mid-afternoon is oily. Skin that stings or reddens easily is sensitive on top of whichever of those it is. Balanced is the one that mostly behaves itself.</p>",
            "set_piece": "finder",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_what_is_the_difference_between_flow_core_and": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Flow, Core and Deep?",
            "answer": "<p>How much cold-pressed oil each one carries. In the current formulations, that is the only thing that changes.</p> <p>Flow is over 9% plant oils, sinks in quickly and is made for the face. Core is over 14%, richer and more cushioning, made for the body. Deep is over 19%, the substantial one for hands, elbows, knees and feet.</p> <p>Within a skin type, all three share the same oils, the same prebiotic and the same pH. You are choosing by where you are putting it and how rich you like it to feel.</p>",
            "set_piece": "textures",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_my_face_and_my_body_are_not_the_same_do_i_ne": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My face and my body are not the same. Do I need two?",
            "answer": "<p>You may well want two. Skin on the face and body behaves differently, and Flow on the face with Core on the body is a sensible pairing. Nothing in the range conflicts, so mixing is fine.</p><p>If you are starting with one, buy for your face. It is the skin you will notice first.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_is_it_suitable_for_sensitive_skin": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it suitable for sensitive skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Two of the five types are built for it, Dry Sensitive and Oily Sensitive. There is no synthetic fragrance anywhere in the range.</p><p>We publish every ingredient and every percentage on every product page, so if there is something your skin has fallen out with before, you can check for it before you buy rather than after.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "ethos-gentle",
            "ethos_label": "Made to be gentle on skin"
          }
        },
        "cat_using_it": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Using it"
          }
        },
        "q_how_do_i_use_it": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Warm a small amount between your fingertips and press it into clean skin, morning or night or both, before any make-up or sunscreen. On the body, massage it in until it disappears.</p> <p>Small amount is the operative phrase. These are concentrated, and it is easy to use twice what you need at first.</p>",
            "set_piece": "dose",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_how_long_before_i_notice_anything": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice anything?",
            "answer": "<p>You will feel the moisture as soon as it goes on. Anything longer-term takes more time, because skin renews its surface roughly every four weeks, and more slowly with age. You are waiting on new cells rather than changing the ones already there.</p><p>Give it a fortnight to see how it suits you. That is why the trial runs for two weeks.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_can_i_use_it_under_sunscreen_or_make_up": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use it under sunscreen or make-up?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Flow absorbs the fastest, so it suits wearing under both, and Core is not far behind. Give it a minute to absorb before the next layer goes on.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_should_i_patch_test_first": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Should I patch test first?",
            "answer": "<p>If your skin reacts easily, yes. A small amount on the inner forearm, left for 24 hours, tells you most of what you need to know. If your skin is generally uneventful, you can skip it.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_how_long_does_a_bottle_last_and_how_long_doe": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does a bottle last, and how long does it keep once opened?",
            "answer": "<p>A 150ml bottle used twice a day on the face lasts around three months. On the body it goes faster, because there is more of you.</p> <p>Once opened, use it within six months. That is the small open-jar symbol on the bottle with 6M beside it. The batch number and date are on the base.</p>",
            "set_piece": "bottle_base",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
