        "q_rosacea_or_eczema": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I have rosacea or eczema. Can I use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Our moisturisers are cosmetics, so they are not a treatment for any skin condition. Dry Sensitive and Oily Sensitive are formulated for skin that tends to dryness, redness and reactivity, and every ingredient and its percentage is published, so you can check it against anything your skin has reacted to before.</p><p>If you are under the care of a doctor or dermatologist, check with them first, and patch test before first use.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_where_is_it_made": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where is it made, and where does the seaweed come from?",
            "answer": "<p>Everything is made by hand, in small batches, in Welcombe on the north Devon coast. The bladderwrack in every product is the same Atlantic seaweed species that grows on the rocks below Welcombe. Ours is a cold infusion in sunflower oil, made in the UK by O&amp;3.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_samples_or_smaller_sizes": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you do samples or smaller sizes?",
            "answer": "<p>Not at the moment. The <a href=\"/policies/refund-policy\">Two-Week Trial</a> is there for the same reason: if a product does not suit you, we will swap it or refund it.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_what_is_the_bottle_without_a_pump": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the bottle without a pump, and why is it only a pound less?",
            "answer": "<p>It is the same 150ml aluminium bottle with the same cream in it, without the pump. The pump is the only plastic part, and it is made to move from bottle to bottle.</p><p>A pound is roughly what the pump costs us, so the saving is the pump coming off the price rather than a reward for buying less.</p><p>If this is your first order, buy the version with the pump. A bottle on its own is one you cannot easily get the cream out of.</p>",
            "set_piece": "refill_pair",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        },
        "q_why_no_spf": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is there no SPF in your moisturisers?",
            "answer": "<p>Because a moisturiser goes on too thinly to give the protection an SPF number promises. The SPF on a label is measured with 2mg of product on every square centimetre of skin, which is a thick layer. Research at King's College London found that people apply less than half that, and at that thickness an SPF 50 sunscreen gave at best 40% of the protection on its label. Our moisturisers are concentrated and made to be used in small amounts, so an SPF added to them would fall shorter still.</p><p>Sun protection also needs topping up. The <a href=\"https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/seasonal-health/sunscreen-and-sun-safety/\">NHS</a> advises reapplying sunscreen every two hours, and after swimming, sweating or towelling. A moisturiser you put on at breakfast is not something you reapply through the day, which is why <a href=\"https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/causes-of-cancer/sun-uv-and-cancer/ways-to-enjoy-the-sun-safely\">Cancer Research UK</a> advises using a sunscreen even when your moisturiser contains SPF.</p><p>So our moisturisers do one job, and you choose how to handle the sun. That might be a sunscreen of SPF 30 or higher with at least four-star UVA protection, a mineral one based on zinc oxide if you prefer a simpler formula, and shade, a hat and covering clothing, which the NHS recommends alongside sunscreen. Put the moisturiser on first and give it a minute to absorb before your sunscreen goes on. Nothing in our products protects against the sun.</p>",
            "set_piece": "none",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "ethos_label": ""
          }
        }
      },
